course: dictionary
lesson: 5727
title: Precise words paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words do more work than others. «We had a nice cake at the nice party and it was nice» tells the reader almost nothing. One precise word, like lopsided, paints a picture in the reader's mind straight away.
explain: Lopsided means leaning to one side, with one side bigger, lower or heavier than the other. When Chloe bakes a lopsided cake, you can picture it tilting, not just guess that it looks bad. Ask yourself: what does this word show me that a plain word would not?
explain: Lopsided can also describe a result. A lopsided game is one where the teams are very unequal, so one side wins easily. Sports writers use it for scores that are not even at all.
explain: Piling up words like big, huge, enormous and massive does not help much; the reader just waits for the real picture. Choose one exact word instead.
fact: Lopsided means leaning to one side, with one side bigger, lower or heavier than the other.
fact: Lopsided can also mean very unequal, as in a lopsided game or result.
fact: In maths, the opposite of lopsided is symmetrical, which means balanced on both sides.
fact: A lopsided answer in a survey can happen when you ask only one kind of person, such as people in the pizza queue.
fact: One precise word, like lopsided, paints a clearer picture than a pile of vague words like big and nice.
exercise: Chloe bakes a lopsided cake for Aisha. What does lopsided mean here? | Burnt on the outside | Perfectly round and smooth | Very sweet and sticky | *Leaning to one side, with one side bigger or lower than the other
exercise: A football game ends 9 to 0, and one team hardly gets near the goal. Which word describes the result best? | Narrow | Balanced | Gentle | *Lopsided
exercise: In maths, which word is the opposite of lopsided? | Crooked | *Symmetrical | Heavy | Tilted
test: «The old tower stood ___, with one side much lower than the other.» Which word paints the clearest picture? | *lopsided | nice | good | big
test: Ella says the sports result was lopsided. What does she mean? | The game was very quiet | The two teams were exactly equal | *The two teams were very unequal, so one team won easily | The score was hard to read
exam: Why is «We had a nice cake» weaker than «We had a lopsided cake»? | *Because a precise word paints a clearer picture | Because it has more letters | Because nice is a longer word | Because lopsided means nice
